---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Background from "../components/Background.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import { profile } from "../data/profile";

const updated = "October 6, 2026";
---

<Base title="Rohit Bhatia — Terms of Service">
  <div style="position:relative; min-height:100vh;">
    <Background />
    <Nav subpage />

    <div class="legal" style="position:relative; z-index:1;">
      <a href="/" class="page-link" style="font-size:13px; color:var(--muted);">&larr; Back</a>

      <div style="font-family:'Geist Mono',monospace; font-size:15px; margin:28px 0 8px;">
        <span style="color:var(--faint);">&lt;/</span><span style="color:var(--accent);"
          >terms</span
        ><span style="color:var(--faint);">&gt;</span>
      </div>
      <p class="stamp">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <h2>1. What this site is</h2>
      <p>
        This is {profile.name}&rsquo;s personal website &mdash; a r&eacute;sum&eacute;, some notes
        about what I&rsquo;m working on, and a few things I&rsquo;ve built. It is not a product, a
        service, or a company. By browsing it you agree to the terms below. If you don&rsquo;t agree
        with them, the fix is simple: close the tab.
      </p>

      <h2>2. No account, no payment</h2>
      <p>
        There is nothing to sign up for and nothing to buy. If a page ever asks you for a password
        or a card number, it isn&rsquo;t mine &mdash; don&rsquo;t type anything in.
      </p>

      <h2>3. The content is my opinion, as of the day I wrote it</h2>
      <p>
        Everything here is written in a personal capacity. It is not the position of any employer,
        past or present. I write things down when they&rsquo;re true and I don&rsquo;t always go
        back and update them, so treat anything undated as possibly stale. None of it is
        professional, legal, or financial advice.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Use it, but don&rsquo;t pass it off as yours</h2>
      <p>
        Read it, quote it, link to it, send it to a friend. If you quote more than a line or two,
        credit me and link back. What you shouldn&rsquo;t do: republish whole pages as your own,
        use my name or writing to imply I endorse something I don&rsquo;t, or feed the content into
        something that presents it as its own work. Code I publish is governed by whatever license
        ships with that repository, not by this page.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Automated access</h2>
      <p>
        Crawlers and agents are welcome &mdash; there&rsquo;s a <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> and
        an agent-facing view precisely because I expect them. Please keep requests to a sane rate,
        identify yourself honestly in your user agent, and don&rsquo;t try to get at anything that
        isn&rsquo;t being served publicly. Scraping with intent to impersonate me is not welcome.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Links out</h2>
      <p>
        I link to GitHub, LinkedIn, a scheduling page, and other people&rsquo;s work. Once you
        follow a link you&rsquo;re on someone else&rsquo;s site under someone else&rsquo;s rules,
        and I have no control over what you find there.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Getting in touch is not a contract</h2>
      <p>
        Booking time on my calendar or emailing me starts a conversation, nothing more. No
        employment relationship, engagement, or obligation on either side comes out of it. If you
        send me an unsolicited idea, I can&rsquo;t promise to keep it confidential &mdash; so
        don&rsquo;t send me anything you&rsquo;d be upset to see independently.
      </p>

      <h2>8. No warranty, no liability</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided as-is. I don&rsquo;t promise it will be up, correct, or free of
        mistakes, and I&rsquo;m not liable for anything that follows from your using it or relying
        on it. Where the law doesn&rsquo;t allow that to be excluded, my liability is limited to the
        smallest amount the law permits.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        I may edit these terms. The date at the top is the only changelog. Continuing to use the
        site after a change means you accept the current version.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a>. I read everything, and I
        answer most of it.
      </p>

      <p class="stamp" style="margin-top:40px;">
        See also the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 24px 96px;
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-e4);
    margin: 36px 0 10px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .legal p {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-c8);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .legal .stamp {
    font-family: "Geist Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .legal a:not(.page-link) {
    color: var(--text-9);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
</style>
